  "why": "A river in its own valley: terrain with a riverbed and a waterBody river, the bridge standing on the two banks. A plank snaps under a loaded cart, stone piers and a long slab replace it, the slab cracks, and an arch is built stone by stone over a wooden frame up to its keystone; the weight runs down the curve into the piers, the frame is pulled away and a road, walls and a rolling cart finish it. The camera frames the plank, then holds the bridge's front across the river.",
